Terraform Commands and Practice

1. Introduction

Terraform provides command-line tools for initializing, checking, planning, applying, and removing infrastructure configurations.

During my internship learning, I practiced the basic Terraform commands and understood their purpose in the Infrastructure as Code workflow.

2. Terraform Init

The `terraform init` command initializes a Terraform working directory.

It prepares the directory and downloads the required provider plugins.

Command:

terraform init

3. Terraform Validate

The `terraform validate` command checks whether the Terraform configuration is syntactically valid and internally consistent.

Command:

terraform validate

4. Terraform Format

The `terraform fmt` command formats Terraform configuration files into a consistent style.

Command:

terraform fmt

5. Terraform Plan

The `terraform plan` command shows the changes Terraform intends to make to the infrastructure.

Command:

terraform plan

It allows the configuration changes to be reviewed before applying them.

6. Terraform Apply

The `terraform apply` command applies the configuration and creates or modifies the required infrastructure.

Command:

terraform apply

Terraform displays the planned changes before applying them.

7. Terraform Destroy

The `terraform destroy` command removes the infrastructure managed by the Terraform configuration.

Command:

terraform destroy

This command should be used carefully because it can remove managed resources.

8. Basic Terraform Workflow

The basic workflow I practiced was:

Create Configuration
        ↓
terraform init
        ↓
terraform fmt
        ↓
terraform validate
        ↓
terraform plan
        ↓
terraform apply
        ↓
Check Resources
        ↓
terraform destroy

9. Basic Command Summary

Command | Purpose

terraform init | Initialize the Terraform working directory

terraform fmt | Format Terraform configuration

terraform validate | Validate the configuration

terraform plan | Preview infrastructure changes

terraform apply | Apply the configuration

terraform destroy | Remove managed infrastructure

10. Practice with AWS

I studied the basic workflow of using Terraform with AWS.

The general process is:

Terraform Configuration
        ↓
AWS Provider
        ↓
Terraform Plan
        ↓
Terraform Apply
        ↓
AWS Resource

This helped me understand how Infrastructure as Code can be used to manage cloud resources.

11. Learning Outcome

Through this practice, I became familiar with the most commonly used Terraform commands and understood their role in the Infrastructure as Code workflow.

I also learned how to initialize, format, validate, preview, apply, and remove Terraform-managed infrastructure.
